# PrimusScope: current discovery target is BSC (chain 56), Etherscan API V2.
# This is a template, NOT the active Codex cloud environment-variable store.
# Never put a real key in this tracked example or paste it into chat.
# In Codex: Edit environment -> Environment variables -> Manage.
# Create ETHERSCAN_API_KEY there and add api.etherscan.io to allowed domains.
# Discovery scripts read process environment; they do not load this file.

# The ONLY required variable for the current BSC discovery test:
ETHERSCAN_API_KEY=

# Optional local indexed mode; npm dev:indexed/start:indexed set these for the
# child process automatically, so no managed environment edit is needed.
# PRIMUSSCOPE_DATA_MODE=indexed
# PRIMUSSCOPE_DB_PATH=/absolute/path/to/PrimusScope/.local/indexer.sqlite
# SQLite is local persistence; indexed serving refuses an unconfigured Vercel
# runtime rather than treating its filesystem as a durable database.

# Hosted deployment: configure in the respective Vercel production project,
# not in the Codex environment or this example. Never copy real values here.
# Public web project only:
# PRIMUSSCOPE_DATA_MODE=hosted
# WEB_DATABASE_URL=
# Separate collector project only:
# WORKER_DATABASE_URL=
# CRON_SECRET=
# Administrative provider credentials are bootstrap-only, never web runtime.

# Deployment automation only if token-based Vercel authentication is selected:
# VERCEL_TOKEN=
# IDs can be discovered after linking; not manual prerequisites now:
# VERCEL_ORG_ID=
# VERCEL_PROJECT_ID=

# Optional future direct BSC reads, not required for Etherscan discovery:
# BNB_RPC_URL=https://bsc-rpc.publicnode.com

# Base research is separate zkTLS Network coverage, not this finance workflow.
# BASE_RPC_URL=https://base-rpc.publicnode.com
# BASE_RPC_FALLBACK_URL=

# Primus/connector/monitoring credentials are feature-dependent and intentionally
# not requested before the supported integration is selected and validated.
